  "observed": {
    "summary": "All four stems share the global timeline origin: each is mono 16-bit 44.1 kHz and its length equals its last note end on the global timeline (1.5, 2.0, 2.5, 3.0 s at 120 BPM, within one frame), so leading silence is preserved and nothing is trimmed to the first note. The Lead, Baritone and Bass stems contain exact digital silence (all-zero samples) until 0.4000, 0.9000 and 1.4000 s: their audio begins about 0.1 s (measured 93 to 97 ms from a 2 ms RMS onset) before the expected entrance at 0.5, 1.0 and 1.5 s. The Tenor, whose entrance is at 0, has audio from the first sample. No stem extends to the 4.0 s song end, and none has a tail beyond its last note end.",
