  "classification": "MATCH",
  "classification_note": "Stems preserve the global timeline origin for OpenUtau 0.1.565 with this bank: leading silence equals the entrance (minus a roughly 0.1 s early onset that is a synthesis property), and stems end at their own last note end, so a mixer needs to pad the end to the performed length and needs no per-stem start offsets for origin. UNKNOWN, not resolved: the cause of the roughly 0.1 s early onset (consistent with UTAU preutterance but not verified, and singer dependent); and whether the Tenor first note, which starts at time 0, is clipped or shifted rather than having the same pre-note region.",
